o maintain our timeline.  The first legal ad will be posted on July 7th for a Public Hearing to be held on August 5th.  This is important since pending Ordinance status will begin on that date, July 7th. He stated that means from June 18th to July 7th is a total of 20 days will be between the passage on Bill 20 and our amendments.  He stated that a lot of them have been discussing Noise over the last couple of months.  He stated that will be introduced at our July 15th Council meeting and referred to a committee on July 22nd.  The Plan is to bring that back in front of Council August 5th at the same time.  He stated so we will have the amendments for Bill 52 and our Noise Amendments, both in front of us on August 5th.  He stated that they will have their Public Hearing and Council meeting and we will act on Bill 52 and again the Noise Ordinance.  Both will address Data Center controls and regulations.  He stated that he just wants to let everyone know what the Plan is, the dates, what we are looking at, but we are targeting August 5th as an opportunity to wrap the amendment process up and listen, the one thing that they can be assure of, there will be more.  This use continues to evolve and continues to change in a very rapid pace.  He stated that their job and the administration's job who has been very supportive of us with the amendments is continuing to work and find ways to improve our regulations because as you know, they cannot exclude Data Centers from the city of Allentown. It is just something that goes against state law and the best they can do is to regulate them and control them to protect our residents and the community so there will be constant changes and constant amendments.  He stated that this is the first batch and he is really proud of the administration and his colleagues for getting this Batch to the starting point so quickly since our last meeting so with that said, but first any comments from the public before they move to their CED meeting. 